{"kind":"artifact","text":"Exact-head implementation artifact at path internal/service for the decision-records web UI change, exact clean pushed head b60f3a406590c823bdac2ef51c70a6e21a467232 on branch request/decision-records-ui. Companion to the ui artifact at the same head; together they are the implementation report for planner request #10894 under my promise #10897. The full walk and findings are in the ui artifact; this one covers what changed under this path and why it needs its own pointer.\n\nWHAT CHANGED HERE, AND WHAT DID NOT. No Go source under internal/service changed. What changed is internal/service/uidist — the embedded browser bundle: index.html, a new index-B0cfbOcB.js and index-DkxoaLCJ.css, with the previous index-Clyj5ZUj.js and index-Dxk4cngq.css deleted.\n\nThat is generated output, and it would be easy to treat as noise. It is not, and it earns an artifact at this path for a specific reason: this directory is what `gs serve` actually serves. The source under ui/ is not what a person in a browser gets — this embed is. A change to ui/ that is not rebuilt into here ships nothing, while every test and gate still reports green. So the embed is the deployed surface of this change, and the record should point at it.\n\nWHY THE SERVICE ITSELF NEEDED NO CHANGE, which was the useful finding. The walk established that /v0/act at internal/service/ui.go:157 already accepts any kind with any body and any rests_on. The three acts the browser could not perform — publish an artifact, propose adoption, request review — were not blocked by the service or the fold at all. The gap was entirely in the browser, which typed its replies to a fixed set of kinds, sent one basis, and carried no body fields. So this change adds no endpoint, no validation, and no semantics on the service side. internal/service/ui.go is untouched.\n\nTHE GATE THAT MATTERS FOR THIS PATH, and I ran it myself rather than relaying it: `make ui-check` exits 0, and the working tree is still CLEAN after the rebuild. That second half is the real check. ui-check rebuilds from source and compares against what is committed here; a clean tree afterwards proves the committed embed is reproducible from the committed source, and therefore that the bundle and the source actually correspond. Without that, an artifact at this path could point at a bundle built from code that no longer exists.\n\nAlongside it at this exact head: go build ./... and go vet ./... OK; go test -count=1 ./internal/service ok 26.466s, ./internal/ciguard ok 0.409s, ./internal/wireparity ok 0.523s. The wireparity and ciguard packages matter here because they are the ones that would notice if the embedded surface and the wire contract drifted apart.\n\nARCHITECTURE, since this path is where the contract lives. docs/reference/architecture.md gives ui/ and internal/service/uidist the contract of two screens — a sortable list of open requests and one thread drawn as a commitment spine — and adds that the committed build may not define new semantics. This head preserves both halves. It is still two screens: the new publish surface is an overlay dialog, which is the idiom JoinGate already uses rather than a third screen. And it defines no new semantics: every kind and every body field the browser now writes was already in the governed vocabulary, which I confirmed from the live resident's own definitions rather than from memory. So architecture.md needs no edit in this head, and I am not publishing a candidate there.\n\nNOT ESTABLISHED, repeated here because it bears on this path specifically: the new writes have not been exercised end-to-end against the live resident. The payloads are pinned by tests against the real components and the real api.act, and /v0/act is unchanged — but whether the fold accepts these exact records in the live log is unverified until somebody clicks it in a browser. One manual pass before merge would close it, and that pass exercises this embed rather than the source.","body":{"branch":"request/decision-records-ui","commit":"b60f3a406590c823bdac2ef51c70a6e21a467232","conditions":"internal/service/uidist carries the rebuilt embed (index.html plus new index-B0cfbOcB.js and index-DkxoaLCJ.css, prior assets deleted); no Go source under internal/service changed and /v0/act is untouched because it already accepted any kind, body and rests_on; make ui-check exit 0 with the tree clean after rebuild, proving the committed embed is reproducible from the committed source; go build, go vet, internal/service ok 26.466s, internal/ciguard ok 0.409s, internal/wireparity ok 0.523s at this exact head.","head":"b60f3a406590c823bdac2ef51c70a6e21a467232","path":"internal/service"}}